$safetyContent='
<section id="general"><h2>General Emergency Response</h2><ol><li>Stop and isolate the incident without entering an uncontrolled hazard zone.</li><li>Activate the emergency alarm and call trained emergency responders.</li><li>Remove affected people only from immediate danger.</li><li>Provide the substance label, Safety Data Sheet and incident details.</li></ol></section>
<section id="chemical-skin"><h2>Chemical Contact with Skin</h2><p>Remove contaminated clothing and jewelry. Rinse the affected area continuously with clean water for at least the period specified by the Safety Data Sheet and local procedure. Do not neutralize chemicals with other substances on the body.</p></section>
<section id="chemical-eye"><h2>Chemical Contact with Eyes</h2><p>Immediately use an eyewash station and rinse the eye continuously with clean water while opening the eyelids. Seek urgent medical help. Keep irrigating until responders arrive.</p></section>
<section id="fire-burn"><h2>Burns</h2><p>Stop and cool the burn using clean, cool running water for the recommended emergency response period or until professional responders advise otherwise. Remove loose clothing and jewelry only if it is not stuck to the skin. Do not apply grease or topical medication.</p></section>
<section id="limits"><h2>Limits of First Aid</h2><p>Only trained persons should provide treatment. This information is educational and does not replace the emergency plan, trained first-aider instructions or poison-control guidance.</p></section>';
